",294,"a"],[0.6909,1,215,58,0,8,25,85,"a",294,"a"],[0.708,1,134,54,0,3,20,114,"a",294,"a"],[0.7291,1,174,58,12,1,23,210,"a",78,"a"],[0.7297,1,99,41,3,1,16,39,"a",177,"a"],[0.7299,1,155,59,1,3,26,85,"a",78,"a"],[0.7305,1,153,46,0,2,20,49,"a",78,"a"],[0.7534,1,175,67,1,6,27,104,"a",294,"a"],[0.7644,1,301,57,1,2,46,52,"a",417,"a"],[0.7694,1,69,52,0,0,14,-1,"",78,"a"],[0.787,1,74,46,0,0,16,-1,"",43,"d"],[0.7997,1,140,59,1,5,21,104,"a",294,"a"],[0.7997,1,325,54,0,2,47,416,"a",417,"a"],[0.7998,1,69,52,3,0,16,-1,"",78,"a"],[0.8021,1,79,46,0,0,19,-1,"",177,"a"],[0.813,1,216,39,1,1,25,85,"a",294,"a"],[0.8192,1,90,56,0,1,17,104,"a",78,"a"],[0.8215,1,75,44,2,0,19,-1,"",392,"a"],[0.8319,1,299,57,1,3,48,114,"a",417,"a"],[0.834,1,103,50,0,2,24,104,"a",177,"a"],[0.8361,1,195,63,6,3,32,210,"a",452,"a"],[0.8365,1,129,41,0,0,28,-1,"",294,"a"],[0.8835,1,137,43,0,0,26,-1,"",177,"a"],[0.906,1,117,26,1,0,26,-1,"",294,"a"],[0.9192,1,325,52,0,1,56,79,"a",417,"a"],[0.9258,1,251,55,0,0,54,-1,"",417,"a"],[0.9539,1,300,45,1,0,59,-1,"",417,"a"],[0.9548,1,328,51,6,1,58,313,"a",417,"a"],[0.9852,1,174,43,0,0,30,-1,"",78,"a"],[1.0,1,215,47,0,0,36,-1,"",294,"a"]],"texts":{"8":"Migration keeps my workplace and my community going. Cutting it back would cost us more than it would save.","22":"Migration is about people, not just workers. Families being able to live together should count as much as economic contribution.","27":"If we expect newcomers to learn English, classes and settlement support should be funded for everyone, not just permanent arrivals.","34":"As a lucky country, we have a duty to keep helping people who aren't so lucky, even when it costs us.","39":"Reducing migrant discourse solely to whether they use finite resources or can contribute via their labour reduces their humanity","40":"People would be less racist and more trusting of immigrants if they knew how badly Australia needs some of the skills - facts and numbers.","41":"Migration debates are often a thinly veiled excuse to indulge in racism","43":"This whole discussion is contrived by the hard right for political division. It's a repeat of their tactics in the Voice referendum.","44":"Politic is driving this discussion and creating unnecessary division. Let's celebrate our multicultural nation.","45":"We have a responsibility to welcome and offer refuge to asylum seekers and refugees. We take only 20,000 per year that's abysmal.","47":"The real question is, are we a generous and open society or selfish, greedy and xenophobic creating excuses to question immigration.","49":"For political representatives, decency, what's right, fair and generous (humanist) must be how you respond even if your electors disagree.","51":"Migrants make an outsized contribution to the community because they tend to be highly motivated and entrepreneurial by necessity","52":"There should be no bias towards any particular country of origin in migrant qualification criteria","78":"Immigration should be discriminatory. We should only take the best.","79":"A bigger Australia is a richer Australia with more employers, workers, wealth and resources for all","83":"There is already plenty of factual information about how migration works, people choose to ignore it because they'd prefer to blame migrants","85":"Migration debate can often be centred around xenophobia and racism, which is not helpful.","89":"People complain about migrants living with their own community but refuse to allow more houses to be built in their suburbs for migrants","98":"Some of the recent immigration debate is just thinly disguised racism","104":"Migration plays an unacknowledged but important role in supporting economic growth (which safeguards against recession)","114":"It needs to be much easier to get qualifications recognised from overseas in Australia.","132":"We should focus on building trust and unity across communities rather than simply cutting migration.","173":"more stories would help us to understand what it is to be a migrant","177":"Australia is too lax on who can gain permanent residency / citizenship.","197":"Migrant work ethic is what has built this nation since 1788.  Give us the tools and the knowledge and it will happen.","199":"The truth is new businesses start via migrants and most people forget this is helpful to the ecomony","210":"Unless you are indigenous, your ancestors were ALL migrants, so let's welcome newcomers to our lucky country","214":"We should welcome skilled migrants only if they are already sponsored by an employer.","217":"Most of the cultural or social concerns about migration would be alleviated by a smaller, slower migration program (100k)","273":"Social cohesion issues are driven by domestic tribalism within Australia; migration's a convenient scapegoat.","294":"We should be selecting migrants based on both their proven skills and countries with a high cultural and religious integration success rate.","299":"Migration is an economic imperative with a declining fertility rate and an ageing population.","313":"The governments cap of student visas not only damages the university sector, but students also pay rent, tax and do jobs others will not do.","329":"My son is denied work, any entry level, retail job he applies. No chance because only hire Asian or South Asian. Migration takes away jobs.","385":"We dont need more regulation, or programs. The individual needs to do their own work to learn English.","392":"I feel like a foreigner in my own home. There are too many communities not assimilating. Mass immigration does not allow integration.","414":"New migrants do not have any affinity or bond with our history and thus no value is placed on heritage homes and places.","415":"There are only so many marbles one can fit into a jar before it is full. Our country can only support a finite number of people. We are full","416":"As a comparatively wealthy country we have a strong obligation to take in and support a wholesome number of true refugees","417":"Why does our Government think a Big Australia Policy is a good idea?  Zero migration during Covid did not hurt Australia.","426":"Migrants and their Australian born offspring from certain cultures account for disproportionately high crime and terrorism offences","433":"More than half my neighbours speak Mandarin.  I dont feel at home in my own neighbourhood. Is Australia a country or just an economic zone?","452":"Immigration levels have been too high leading to stress on services and the housing crisis.","453":"We have allowed too many elderly immigrants on family reunion visas that are not contributing to the economy or integrating with community."},"nsplit":59}</script>
